# Authoring for the autopoet brain — the emission contract + the cage

The autopoet's brain (planner + drafter) edits its own body of `.work` files. This
skill pins the contract the runtime actually enforces — mined from the first live
eval transcripts (27 runs): drafts held the format, but plan rounds half-knew the
emission markers and the `NEED:` lane went unused 27/27 times. Born under the lint
gate: the triad fields and every grantable capability below are extracted from
source by `ci/skills-lint.exs` — this page cannot silently drift.

**When to use:** any time the brain plans or drafts a change to the body; any time
an internal agent writes `.work` for the autopoet.

## The emission contract (exact, or the change is lost)
The drafter's output is parsed for file blocks — nothing else lands:

    === file: <relative-path>.work ===
    <complete file content>

    === append: <relative-path>.work ===
    <lines added at the END — the safe mode; existing content never reproduced>

- Marker is `=== file:` / `=== append:` exactly — never `--- path ---`, never a
  fence. Plan-round prose describing a change does NOT apply it; only the draft's
  blocks do.
- Prefer `append` — placeholder-stub clobbering is impossible by construction.
- No HTML, no markdown code fences, no JSON in `.work` output.

## Ask before guessing (progressive disclosure)
If a guide page is needed to plan correctly, reply with ONLY `NEED: <page>` lines
(max 3). The index is always in context; the pages load into a second round.
Unused disclosure is wasted context accuracy — ask.

## The structural triad (human-gated, never autonomous)
Three fields route ANY change to a human — the cage, enforced by the Gate at merge
time, not by convention: `grant`, `ceiling`, `management`.

- Widening an agent's `grant` — or birthing a NEW agent that carries one — is held
  as a PENDING proposal. Direct writes of armed agents never land.
- A `frozen` agent is never autonomously editable; a `proposed` one always routes
  to a human; `management` self-promotion is refused.
- `ceiling` changes in `index.work` are structural acts — human-gated.

## Grantable capabilities (the REAL vocabulary — anything else is dropped, not trusted)
`net`, `kv`, `secrets`, `fs`, `exec`, `llm`, `browse`, `queue`, `vfs`, `commands`,
`tcp`, `udp`, `tls`, `posix`, `parallel`, `encode`.

An agent block that needs power declares it:

    agent :clerk do
      prompt "file what lands, keep receipts"
      grant net
    end

## Reactive + time (exact shapes)
    hook :name do
      match tags: [:some_tag]
      notify
    end

`trigger every: "1h"` (or `cron`/`at`) may ride a hook for time-driven work.
Dates are org timestamps only — `<2026-07-04 Sat>` — never invented, never
reformatted.
